5. Complex assignments (`$i = $i - 1`) created two Store nodes due to SPPF ambiguity

## User Message 5: "the ambiguity should be ok, either they'll create identical node structures and we can trim one or the parse will naturally disambiguate later, or we will have to provide an optimization to disambiguate later ... the SPPF structure is there specifically to handle ambiguous cases"

Critical feedback: Don't fight SPPF ambiguity, embrace it. This changed my approach completely.

My response:
