It's checking `$chart{$item}` not `$chart{$item->key}`. This is using the $item object as a hash key, which will stringified to the key via the overload.

But in add_element, we're using:
```perl
my $key = $item->key;
my $current = $self->get_element($key);
```

So has_item($new_item) is equivalent to exists($chart{$new_item->key}).

